event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":75,"item_id":"rs_00f8533f2aca44c2016acabaacc8a481979e5de6738c638c6d","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering database options**\n\nI’m thinking about how to simplify the rememberPosition function without having an ON conflict, since creating new movements should be fine. It seems migration or ignoring quietly could also work for potential conflicts, but that might only happen with invalid or nonstandard databases. I can see that an update to the documentation will be necessary to clarify how this should all work together."}

