d there. Returning to a previous project restores its remembered position relative to that project's other tasks, even if multiple tasks return in a different order. Moves preserve identity, title, completion, priority, and due date; returning never restores older field values.\"},{\"oldText\":\"Per-project task ordering is persisted independently from task IDs, with existing databases migrated in their original creation order. New tasks append after moved tasks, and moves survive restarts and can be repeated.\",\"newText\":\"Per-project task positions are persisted independently from task IDs and remain reserved while a task is elsewhere. New tasks and first-time arrivals append after all reserved positions, including absent tasks. Existing databases migrate their current task order unchanged; historical ownership before this migration cannot be reconstructed. Position history and current ownership are saved atomically, survive restarts, and remain intact through project renaming, archival, and restoration.\"},{\"oldText\":\"blank and saved dates, repeated moves, and restart persistence.\",\"newText\":\"blank and saved dates, repeated moves, and restart persistence. Return-order tests cover reverse returns, reserved slots in empty projects, independent histories across three projects, current-field preservation, archive/restore, renaming, and migration from existing non-ID task order.\"}]}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","offset","limit"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command","timeout"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d05f0b6a-e641-4060-910c-20bd1efae1d1","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"medium","summary":"detailed","context":"all_turns","mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18495,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":358,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":39},"total_tokens":18853,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba61ffdc81979e01cab7241408ab":{"input_tokens":38,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba641d8481979871c77de731df04":{"input_tokens":28,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba65fdb88197b89ab07d8170f64b":{"input_tokens":33,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba680ff08197a4ac1e12900a29ec":{"input_tokens":44,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba69239c81978ff20d7e34017493":{"input_tokens":22,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00f8533f2aca44c2016acaba69239c8197a85e7a71c3a3490f":{"input_tokens":24,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_